(Ateliers du Rhône  Structural appraisal of the existing frame) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prepared for DBS Architectes · August 2026) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Scope) Tj T*
(Appraisal of the existing reinforced concrete frame of the former) Tj T*
(warehouse at Ateliers du Rhône, to establish capacity for the proposed) Tj T*
(change of use to studios and workshops.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Existing construction) Tj T*
(The frame is in-situ reinforced concrete on a 6.0 by 7.2 m grid, built) Tj T*
(in 1962. Slabs are 180 mm one-way spanning. Columns are 400 by 400 mm.) Tj T*
(Foundations are pad bases, assumed 1.8 m square from trial holes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Condition) Tj T*
(Cover meter survey found cover between 18 and 34 mm against a nominal) Tj T*
(25 mm. Carbonation depth averaged 11 mm. Chloride content is below the) Tj T*
(threshold. Two areas of spalling were noted at the east elevation, both) Tj T*
(associated with rainwater goods rather than systemic corrosion.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Capacity) Tj T*
(Existing slab capacity is 3.0 kN/m2 imposed. The proposed workshop use) Tj T*
(requires 5.0 kN/m2. Strengthening is required to bays B3 to B6 and C3) Tj T*
(to C6. Carbon fibre plate bonded to the soffit is recommended.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. New openings) Tj T*
(The proposed stair opening at grid B4 requires trimming. A steel frame) Tj T*
(picking up on the existing columns is recommended over slab widening.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Conclusions) Tj T*
(The frame is sound and suitable for retention. Strengthening of eight) Tj T*
(bays and local repair of two spalled areas is required. Retention) Tj T*
(avoids an estimated 340 tonnes of embodied carbon against rebuild.) Tj T*
ET
